WEBVTT

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:18.890
I'll put this to good use.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:23.940
I've already called it in.
The rest is up to you.

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:27.440
Best of luck!

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:53.260
Looks like it’s raining again
in this anonymous world

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:56.680
Where crowds prop up
revolutionaries' screeds

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.970
Polarity may as well not exist

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:04.270
Crumbling agony

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:08.270
We erased the dots we stared at

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:11.650
Without connecting them
Filling me with loss

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:17.240
Synthetic Sympathy

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.960
The desire to be revealed and embraced

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:32.300
Even solitude is dissolved
in the reticent sea

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:35.420
Unliberated freedom
leads to senseless crime

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:37.630
Bursting my eardrums

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:40.930
Sympathy
The sentiments to hurt and be kissed

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:45.270
Let the vortex of resonating memories
break free of time

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:50.190
Grasping the end of falsehood
to open our eyes

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:16.510
I called Arata earlier.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:21.390
I told him he could hit you back.

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:25.220
Spare me!
Do you want me to get hit?

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:27.560
I think you could use it.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:39.660
What's wrong?

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.200
I'm sorry. It's work.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:44.330
Is it Arata?

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:46.540
No, someone else.

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:53.790
Pleased to make your acquaintance,
Thirteenth Inspector.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:56.340
My name is Shirogane.

00:02:57.050 --> 00:03:02.430
I am of equal standing to Shizuka Homura,
who gave you that device.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:04.510
What do you want?

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:08.850
Only to urge you
to choose your side more carefully.

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:14.520
My resources are more
abundant than Shizuka's.

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:16.980
How, specifically?

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:19.740
I know about your brother.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:27.160
It's a tip on the case.
Might be bogus, but it's worth following.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:31.040
Isn't it dangerous?
Shouldn't you call Arata?

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:36.130
Like I said, it may be a dead end.
I can handle it myself.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:38.840
You're always doing things yourself!

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:44.760
Promise you'll get help
from Arata if you need it. Deal?

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:46.260
I...

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:49.180
Or is Arata a burden on you?

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:50.270
No!

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:53.940
He's my belay partner.

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:58.900
Don't you ever let go of him, then!

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:01.900
Yeah. I promise.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:12.500
About your brother...

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:17.210
The Homura family
was deeply involved in his death.

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:21.970
Do you really intend
to work for your enemy?

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:24.090
What evidence do you have?

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:29.970
If you want it, come find me
without help from Public Safety.

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:32.310
Oh, I almost forgot to tell you.

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:35.980
I can easily have your wife
returned to the facility.

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:38.190
Think you can threaten me?

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:41.900
I just want you to know
what I am capable of.

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:44.240
I'll be waiting, then.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:51.160
Delete voice.
Activate audio filter.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:54.210
Search ambient noise.

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:58.380
Mechanical noise

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:01.050
The sound of airplane engines...

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:07.010
Identify airlines and airfields
from the engine sounds.

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:10.890
Umm, umm...

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:13.060
Identified.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:18.900
C3 transport aircraft is only used
domestically by Hyper Transport Company.

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:21.900
Their main base of operations
is Ariake Airport.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:35.870
I'm sorry I'm late.

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:40.920
Don't worry.
Was there some kind of trouble?

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:47.550
I had a brief chat
with the new inspector.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:53.890
We will hereby resume the Relation.

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:57.390
Let's begin.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:04.320
I'm thrilled to finally go toe-to-toe
against the heir to the Homura Family,

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:06.990
who developed this system.

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:16.220
Good thing the Kisaragi thing
worked out, huh?

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:17.020
Yes.

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:19.640
Irie sure looked relieved.

00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:24.480
Never took him for the coy type.
Turns your stomach, doesn't it?

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:25.900
Well...

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:30.900
Most people try to hide stuff
that's more important to them.

00:07:31.490 --> 00:07:35.780
But it's just the opposite.
You gotta be open about that stuff.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:37.580
You could say that.

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:54.050
Why'd you want to meet me out here?
It's freezing!

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:57.560
Kisaragi...

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:12.610
Kunizuka's in critical condition?

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:18.540
Comb the area.
This might not be an accident.

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:29.630
Offline? What's going on?

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:37.350
What's happening?

00:08:43.770 --> 00:08:45.850
We've been disconnected?

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:51.990
What the...?

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:58.370
Was this your idea?

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:01.120
What would make you think that?

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:26.310
Let the games begin!

00:09:56.340 --> 00:09:58.260
Check the time table.

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:04.060
Remember our motto?

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:07.350
"Training is always harder
than the execution!"

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:09.400
You think I'd forget?

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:28.830
Can't the party give me some notice
before calling a web meeting?

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:31.630
That lipstick works, Karina.

00:10:32.170 --> 00:10:33.130
Right?

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:36.630
Could it be a present
from a certain someone?

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:39.630
Hey!

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:43.220
Leave as soon as you
check the equipment.

00:10:43.510 --> 00:10:49.140
I know. A latent criminal shouldn't
address the governor of Tokyo so casually.

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:53.440
Touché. You're as sharp
as any analyst should be.

00:10:55.570 --> 00:10:57.530
Governor, watch your Hue.

00:10:58.320 --> 00:10:59.780
She's not a problem.

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:04.370
Ms. Karanomori's Crime Coefficient
is going down. Isn't it?

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:07.500
What gave you that impression?

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:10.670
Your composure when
you said "latent criminal."

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:13.040
Wow! You sounded just like Arata!

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:14.460
Do you think so?

00:11:14.590 --> 00:11:16.500
Is Arata doing well?

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:18.170
He's first rate.

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:19.800
Ms. Karanomori.

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:22.800
Yes? What is it?

00:11:23.470 --> 00:11:26.140
We can't sync to the server.

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:45.580
Is this a drill?

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:48.950
A drill?
But we're stuck in here!

00:12:01.670 --> 00:12:04.470
I'm here, Obata dear.

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:07.760
Took you long enough!

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:09.770
Huh? I'm right on time.

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:13.190
You should be five minutes early,
like an adult!

00:12:13.310 --> 00:12:16.480
You're totally useless!
Now turn around!

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:18.400
Yes, Ma'am.

00:12:19.230 --> 00:12:20.570
Unit Two

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:22.610
Anomaly in the holding cells!

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:25.110
We can't access the cameras.

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:28.620
I can't reach Chief Shimotsuki, either.

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:34.120
We'll get the Dominators.
Bando, get to the holding cells.

00:12:34.540 --> 00:12:36.210
Roger that. Let's go!

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:37.380
Yes, sir!

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:48.850
You are all free.

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:53.390
You may leave or stay, however you please.

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:59.520
That said, you will be disposed of
if you stay.

00:13:00.150 --> 00:13:05.410
So I suggest taking detectives hostage
and escaping to an abandoned zone.

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:08.280
Can we trust him?

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:14.790
Clock's ticking. Make up your minds.

00:13:27.390 --> 00:13:31.970
These are the detectives.
They'll be valuable as hostages.

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:35.310
So, what'll it be?

00:13:35.890 --> 00:13:37.940
He's right!
Now's our chance!

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:39.270
Let's do this!

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:46.900
Weren't you in Heaven's Leap?

00:13:48.030 --> 00:13:49.320
Take a good look.

00:13:49.740 --> 00:13:50.870
Torri S. Aschenbach

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:52.410
Posttraumatic shock

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:58.210
Public Safety killed your founder's agent
Torri with handguns, not Dominators.

00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:02.840
Sibyl hasn't abandoned you.

00:14:05.260 --> 00:14:08.340
God is still watching over you.

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:13.350
Let us honor Torri's wish

00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:17.600
to save God from the clutches
of the Public Safety Bureau!

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:22.020
Let's do it!

00:14:23.270 --> 00:14:24.610
Idiots, all of them!

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:27.240
But this is their choice.

00:14:29.530 --> 00:14:31.240
Same goes for Sibyl's society.

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:35.080
In the end, you're responsible
for your own actions.

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:39.500
They're going down the road
laid out for them, like sheep.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.000
Make your own path, I say!

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:44.420
Even if it leads to Hell.

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:49.760
What?

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:21.710
Wakey, wakey!
It's showtime, Arata Shindo.

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:26.170
This is no disaster drill, is it?

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:29.470
My device is acting up.
I can't connect.

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:31.550
What the...?

00:15:34.140 --> 00:15:35.050
There they are!

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:48.320
Not bad, kid!

00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:57.660
What in the world is going on?

00:16:03.920 --> 00:16:05.540
Smells like smoke.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:09.800
Let's clean up, lickety-split.

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:15.300
Check Factor 1.

00:16:17.050 --> 00:16:18.470
Now what?

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:22.810
Someone may have hacked the security room.

00:16:22.980 --> 00:16:25.690
If so, then what's offline?

00:16:26.150 --> 00:16:28.900
Everything. The doors, the elevators...

00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:32.200
That just leaves
the emergency exits, huh?

00:16:35.360 --> 00:16:36.950
They're locked, I'm afraid.

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:39.450
Damn!

00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:43.250
What good are emergency exits
when you can't use 'em?

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:48.920
They were originally set up
to stop latent criminals from escaping.

00:16:49.050 --> 00:16:50.250
Latent criminals?

00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:52.720
Oh, that includes us.

00:16:53.340 --> 00:16:56.430
They could at least set us free
in an emergency!

00:16:56.640 --> 00:17:00.970
Just leave it to me.
This'll take a few minutes.

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:07.690
Stop, Mori!

00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:27.460
I'm sure of it now.

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:29.670
This is an attack.

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:32.210
How could I let this happen?

00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:44.600
Todoroki!

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:47.600
Oh, no! Sorry, Enforcer Todoroki!

00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:14.130
You're with the SAD.

00:18:15.300 --> 00:18:18.130
Sugo's the name.
You helped me with Heaven's Leap.

00:18:21.350 --> 00:18:23.010
Did you tail me?

00:18:23.260 --> 00:18:24.270
Yes.

00:18:24.850 --> 00:18:26.930
What brings you here?

00:18:27.770 --> 00:18:30.100
I'm following up on a tip.

00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:35.440
I'm sorry, but your communications
have been put under surveillance.

00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:36.740
What?

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:40.110
And we didn't intercept any tips.

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:43.410
What means of communication are you using?

00:18:43.780 --> 00:18:45.160
I'm not obliged to say.

00:18:45.450 --> 00:18:47.660
Wire-tapping Public Safety agents?

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:50.120
I'll file a formal complaint.

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:56.670
The SAD has complete jurisdiction
over international cases.

00:18:59.840 --> 00:19:00.890
Come with me.

00:19:01.010 --> 00:19:01.680
I refuse!

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:22.030
Chief! Emergency in progress!
Repeat, emergency in progress!

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:26.040
Latent criminals have escaped.

00:19:26.540 --> 00:19:29.370
Please evacuate to
underground parking ASAP.

00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:31.040
What on Earth?

00:19:31.460 --> 00:19:33.250
Underground parking?

00:19:33.750 --> 00:19:37.050
We can't reach the Chief,
but the intercom works?

00:19:37.380 --> 00:19:38.840
Hurry, Governor!

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:53.190
Hold it!

00:19:53.480 --> 00:19:56.320
This elevator shouldn't
just be waiting for us.

00:19:58.400 --> 00:19:59.940
Get out of there!

00:20:12.620 --> 00:20:13.710
Kunizuka's what?

00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:14.580
Yes.

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:19.460
Don't worry.
I've been told she's going to make it.

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:24.720
First, we'd better
take care of the assailants.

00:20:25.090 --> 00:20:29.850
We'd best consider the server room
and the analysis lab occupied.

00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:34.100
Right. Let's secure the Dominators.

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:38.400
But Storage is on the 20th floor.
That's 35 floors down.

00:20:38.520 --> 00:20:40.280
What other options do we have?

00:20:50.200 --> 00:20:51.120
Where am I?

00:20:55.120 --> 00:20:59.340
The elevator trap sprung.
Factor 1 survived.

00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:02.630
So, she's not gonna be so easy.

00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:06.010
Koichi Azusawa.

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:10.350
Coming here for the governor?
Not a very bright idea.

00:21:12.180 --> 00:21:13.890
Arata Shindo.

00:21:14.140 --> 00:21:19.520
We meet at last, and that's how
you talk to me? You wound me.

00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:22.610
You used foxes, I see.

00:21:22.860 --> 00:21:24.650
There are foxes everywhere.

00:21:25.110 --> 00:21:26.570
Even in Public Safety.

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:32.040
It's what the ancient Chinese called
"an ambush from ten sides."

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:36.290
We've got the governor surrounded.

00:21:36.790 --> 00:21:39.790
So you let us arrest Obata
on purpose, huh?

00:21:40.170 --> 00:21:42.590
Correct. So, you noticed?

00:21:43.170 --> 00:21:44.300
I had a hunch.

00:21:45.050 --> 00:21:47.930
The risk seemed too high
for such small reward.

00:21:50.390 --> 00:21:52.310
Now I see. The paparazzi drones.

00:21:52.430 --> 00:21:55.940
Precisely. But you were too late.

00:21:56.480 --> 00:22:01.820
So you also calculated the time it took
for the drones to be analyzed as evidence.

00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:05.070
Calculation is my strong suit.

00:22:06.150 --> 00:22:10.450
If your Crime Coefficient didn't rise,
there's something wrong with you.

00:22:11.530 --> 00:22:14.700
Easy, there.
I'm more well-adjusted than you.

00:22:14.950 --> 00:22:17.210
Yeah. Well-adjusted and crazy!

00:22:18.870 --> 00:22:22.590
You don't want to kill the governor
you're trying to assassinate.

00:22:25.260 --> 00:22:27.170
I have no interest in doing so.

00:22:27.680 --> 00:22:31.510
This is a test to see if human nature
is in accordance with Sibyl.

00:22:32.260 --> 00:22:33.220
A test?

00:22:33.890 --> 00:22:39.600
The governor will live if she chooses
correctly and shows good citizenship.

00:22:39.900 --> 00:22:42.480
Are you saying you're not doing anything?

00:22:42.940 --> 00:22:46.530
Correct. I simply made
a fork in the road.

00:22:47.150 --> 00:22:51.820
I don't wish for her death, but I'll let
the chips fall where they may.

00:22:55.950 --> 00:22:58.750
That's definitely a sniper turret.

00:23:00.170 --> 00:23:01.250
Use this.

00:23:02.380 --> 00:23:03.420
Thanks.

00:23:07.260 --> 00:23:08.720
I'll draw its fire.

00:23:08.840 --> 00:23:09.880
But you're injured!

00:23:10.680 --> 00:23:12.140
All the more reason.

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:15.470
I'll lose energy
every second I lose blood.

00:23:15.810 --> 00:23:16.770
It's now or never!

00:23:18.270 --> 00:23:19.100
Got it.

00:24:17.740 --> 00:24:19.040
They made it.

00:24:20.200 --> 00:24:21.160
He got away.

00:24:26.130 --> 00:24:28.090
I'm onto the next task. And you?

00:24:28.920 --> 00:24:30.710
Second task, complete.

00:24:31.090 --> 00:24:33.130
I'm off to deal with Factor 2.

00:24:34.430 --> 00:24:36.550
I'll transport Sugo.

00:24:38.390 --> 00:24:39.720
I appreciate this.

00:24:39.970 --> 00:24:41.480
We'll handle the rest.

00:24:42.890 --> 00:24:46.110
I'll trace the turret's operator by air.

00:24:46.560 --> 00:24:48.270
Let me go with you.

00:24:49.440 --> 00:24:53.360
That's fine by me.
But will you be any good to us?

00:24:54.740 --> 00:24:55.700
Of course.

00:24:59.200 --> 00:25:00.240
Fine.

00:25:07.920 --> 00:25:10.050
Emergency lockdown in progress.

00:25:10.750 --> 00:25:13.970
Public access is prohibited.

00:25:15.630 --> 00:25:17.800
I told you, I'm an inspector! Come on!

00:25:18.010 --> 00:25:20.640
No use. It won't accept any inputs.

00:25:21.270 --> 00:25:24.440
Inspector, the press is closing in.

00:25:25.940 --> 00:25:27.690
Keep them away from here.

00:25:33.360 --> 00:25:37.700
This is the Ministry of Welfare
Public Safety Bureau Building.

00:25:38.240 --> 00:25:41.870
Are you out of your mind?

00:25:45.000 --> 00:25:47.420
You can't let your mental state cloud.

00:25:47.790 --> 00:25:50.170
You need a Hue Check and counseling.

00:25:50.290 --> 00:25:51.460
Speak for yourself.

00:25:53.300 --> 00:25:55.010
I'm used to this.

00:25:55.420 --> 00:25:57.970
I'm not that fragile, you know.

00:26:09.980 --> 00:26:10.610
Where are we?

00:26:10.940 --> 00:26:12.610
The waste recovery room.

00:26:13.150 --> 00:26:15.070
There might be something useful.

00:26:21.660 --> 00:26:24.500
Here we go! I can fix this Pillbug up!

00:26:28.420 --> 00:26:30.630
Come on! Why won't this door open?

00:26:31.170 --> 00:26:33.880
Be honest with me. I'll understand.

00:26:34.050 --> 00:26:36.380
I keep telling you, it wasn't me!

00:26:36.670 --> 00:26:39.510
This is an emergency bulletin
from Public Safety.

00:26:41.470 --> 00:26:47.140
Good evening. You are all in a
very tight spot right now.

00:26:48.230 --> 00:26:52.770
This building is completely sealed off
and inaccessible to the outside.

00:26:53.230 --> 00:26:57.150
Moreover, the lower levels are filling
with poisonous gas,

00:26:57.650 --> 00:27:00.530
with hundreds of agents locked inside.

00:27:01.700 --> 00:27:06.410
To boot, the latent criminals
have broken out of the holding cells,

00:27:06.870 --> 00:27:08.790
ready to fight for their freedom.

00:27:09.790 --> 00:27:13.710
You cannot apprehend them.
Unit One is absent inspectors.

00:27:13.840 --> 00:27:15.460
Unit Two has been destroyed.

00:27:15.630 --> 00:27:19.170
Unit Three is locked outside the building,
unable to re-enter.

00:27:20.130 --> 00:27:23.680
The Bureau Chief is in the hands
of foreign mercenaries.

00:27:24.850 --> 00:27:29.020
Inspector Shindo from Unit One
is also being held captive.

00:27:30.390 --> 00:27:34.820
There is only one way
you can be released unharmed.

00:27:35.520 --> 00:27:39.190
Governor Komiya has 30 minutes
to return to the conference room

00:27:39.320 --> 00:27:41.610
and announce her resignation.

00:27:42.320 --> 00:27:43.570
Don't be late!

00:27:44.120 --> 00:27:48.200
In fact, be five minutes early,
since we're all adults.

00:27:49.160 --> 00:27:52.210
Staff will offer full cooperation
with no resistance.

00:27:52.880 --> 00:27:55.210
If not, the hostages will die.

00:27:57.130 --> 00:27:58.760
This is Chief Shimotsuki.

00:27:59.010 --> 00:28:02.220
I'm glad to hear
you're still alive, Chief.

00:28:02.550 --> 00:28:07.720
So you just opened this channel
and closed all outside channels?

00:28:07.930 --> 00:28:10.100
Only for the sake of negotiation.

00:28:10.890 --> 00:28:13.770
We will meet all of your demands.

00:28:14.270 --> 00:28:16.230
Tell me where the governor is.

00:28:16.860 --> 00:28:18.900
That won't do, Chief.

00:28:19.440 --> 00:28:21.490
No stalling for time.

00:28:25.660 --> 00:28:27.120
That cheeky bastard!

00:28:27.830 --> 00:28:29.290
What'll we do, Chief?

00:28:29.540 --> 00:28:31.870
Securing the Dominators is priority one.

00:28:32.330 --> 00:28:36.380
Use your device to check for
surveillance cameras as we move.

00:28:37.590 --> 00:28:41.510
I can't believe Koichi Azusawa
is inside Public Safety.

00:28:41.970 --> 00:28:42.840
What'll we do?

00:28:42.970 --> 00:28:45.140
Do you need to ask? We fight!

00:28:45.640 --> 00:28:48.100
But the shutters look air-tight.

00:28:48.930 --> 00:28:51.140
We're not far from the roof.

00:28:51.600 --> 00:28:53.060
Not far?

00:28:53.690 --> 00:28:55.730
It's 30 floors above us!

00:28:57.900 --> 00:29:01.900
These next 30 minutes
will be fun, huh, Arata?

00:29:02.150 --> 00:29:04.400
Fun? You think this is a game?

00:29:05.700 --> 00:29:07.820
Isn't this society a game?

00:29:08.330 --> 00:29:11.580
It runs on the immutable rules
of the Sibyl System.

00:29:12.330 --> 00:29:16.290
Those who can't fathom its rules
deserve to lose.

00:29:16.500 --> 00:29:19.090
Sibyl provides people
with direction in life.

00:29:19.210 --> 00:29:20.800
It's more than rules to a game.

00:29:21.300 --> 00:29:24.880
Don't you want to be more than a player?

00:29:26.720 --> 00:29:30.060
I just want to be perfect.

00:29:30.310 --> 00:29:31.890
I thought you'd understand.

00:29:33.180 --> 00:29:35.390
We have a lot in common.

00:29:35.690 --> 00:29:38.480
I'm not like you.
We're different in every way!

00:29:39.480 --> 00:29:41.730
No, we have something in common.

00:29:42.730 --> 00:29:44.610
Your father.

00:29:45.240 --> 00:29:49.990
Didn't you become an inspector
to solve your father's death?

00:29:50.580 --> 00:29:52.740
I suggest you give up.

00:29:54.370 --> 00:29:56.460
That man drives people to madness.

00:29:56.580 --> 00:29:57.710
Shut up!

00:29:57.920 --> 00:30:00.750
Dad always fought for others!

00:30:02.710 --> 00:30:05.090
In the Ministry of Welfare's records, yes.

00:30:05.340 --> 00:30:07.970
In actual fact, he was no saint.

00:30:09.390 --> 00:30:14.850
I learned how to use people
as pieces in a game from him.

00:30:15.390 --> 00:30:19.350
Dad wouldn't have used
his mentalist skills for personal gain.

00:30:19.810 --> 00:30:22.730
You're saying the ends justify the means?

00:30:23.230 --> 00:30:28.360
At least he didn't think of no one
but himself, unlike you.

00:30:30.370 --> 00:30:32.330
You just don't get it, do you?

00:30:33.160 --> 00:30:35.040
I don't care about myself.

00:30:35.620 --> 00:30:38.250
I only want to know
the truth about the world.

00:30:59.900 --> 00:31:03.440
Did you learn that Mental Trace
from your father?

00:31:04.520 --> 00:31:05.980
Like father, like son.

00:31:06.150 --> 00:31:09.360
Sadly for you,
my Hue won't cloud any further.

00:31:11.660 --> 00:31:16.290
Your father wanted to be a Congressman.

00:31:18.040 --> 00:31:19.040
As do I.

00:31:19.920 --> 00:31:25.000
But why am I telling you this?
It makes no difference.

00:31:33.430 --> 00:31:34.390
Is he gone?

00:31:41.940 --> 00:31:44.020
Are they jamming communications?

00:31:46.270 --> 00:31:49.030
They only disabled
internal communications.

00:31:49.690 --> 00:31:51.530
We can still send radio waves.

00:31:51.990 --> 00:31:54.570
Our enemy has to control drones, too.

00:31:58.750 --> 00:32:01.290
Do you think we should meet their demands?

00:32:01.830 --> 00:32:05.750
No. That would only make things worse.

00:32:06.340 --> 00:32:08.260
What about that AI of yours?

00:32:09.460 --> 00:32:11.220
Ma-Karina agrees.

00:32:11.590 --> 00:32:15.180
But I can tell that will cloud my Hue.

00:32:15.510 --> 00:32:21.100
If you return, you'll be killed.
If you don't, your Hue will cloud.

00:32:22.020 --> 00:32:25.190
This Azusawa is one twisted man.

00:32:25.900 --> 00:32:26.980
What should I do?

00:32:28.320 --> 00:32:32.450
Leave it to us.
The CID isn't finished yet.

00:32:37.620 --> 00:32:38.660
This is tight.

00:32:42.830 --> 00:32:44.710
Ow...

00:32:51.880 --> 00:32:54.010
The cologne Karina gave me!

00:33:05.020 --> 00:33:06.900
What about those demands?

00:33:07.150 --> 00:33:12.400
The governor has no reason
to announce her resignation.

00:33:13.030 --> 00:33:14.740
He'll kill her on the spot.

00:33:15.160 --> 00:33:18.740
If not personally,
he'll have laid a trap of some kind.

00:33:19.030 --> 00:33:24.250
Agreed. We have to release hostages,
or apprehend the enemy.

00:33:25.080 --> 00:33:30.670
Either way, we have to buy time, restore
the system, and secure the Dominators.

00:33:35.300 --> 00:33:36.470
A Pillbug?

00:33:39.100 --> 00:33:40.510
Good to see you, Chief.

00:33:41.060 --> 00:33:42.020
Shion!

00:33:42.430 --> 00:33:45.980
We made contact.
Now we have a safe line.

00:33:48.020 --> 00:33:51.150
I'm fine. I'm with Karanomori.

00:33:51.480 --> 00:33:53.570
Governor! What a relief!

00:33:54.030 --> 00:33:55.780
Let's check our status.

00:33:56.490 --> 00:34:01.580
Irie, Mao, Arata, and Bureau Chief
Hosorogi are unaccounted for.

00:34:02.450 --> 00:34:03.620
I read you.

00:34:03.750 --> 00:34:06.000
Shion, you account for the others,

00:34:06.120 --> 00:34:09.420
assess the toxic gas spread,
and locate the hostages.

00:34:09.670 --> 00:34:11.130
Can we use Dominators?

00:34:11.420 --> 00:34:13.670
Sure. That should be no problem.

00:34:14.260 --> 00:34:17.300
We'll get our hands on the Dominators.

00:34:17.800 --> 00:34:20.600
Right. Then head to the server room.

00:34:21.470 --> 00:34:27.060
Oh, Chief. I wrote a dummy program
to disrupt the devices' GPS, too.

00:34:27.890 --> 00:34:29.560
Just what we needed, Shion.

00:34:32.230 --> 00:34:35.320
You don't think the first hostage to go

00:34:36.150 --> 00:34:37.900
will be Arata, do you?

00:34:38.450 --> 00:34:40.160
That's highly likely.

00:34:40.620 --> 00:34:42.950
Do you know where he's being held?

00:34:43.370 --> 00:34:47.160
Keep calm. First we have to
check where the gas has spread.

00:34:47.460 --> 00:34:51.960
That'll give us an idea of where
the others are and what routes are safe.

00:34:52.710 --> 00:34:56.970
If we use the Pillbug to access
the biochem weapons defenses...

00:34:57.380 --> 00:34:58.220
There it is.

00:34:58.800 --> 00:35:01.300
The gas goes up to the 20th floor..

00:35:01.510 --> 00:35:04.220
This should lead us to the enemy.

00:35:04.810 --> 00:35:07.600
Because guns and powder
leave a strong smell.

00:35:07.730 --> 00:35:09.190
How'd you know that?

00:35:09.440 --> 00:35:11.860
They use replicas a lot in the movies.

00:35:12.020 --> 00:35:13.360
Nice idea.

00:35:13.690 --> 00:35:16.610
Let's refine the
component analysis filter.

00:35:17.740 --> 00:35:22.200
We got a hit. Not gunpowder,
but high doses of alcohol?

00:35:22.370 --> 00:35:25.740
Dibutylhydroxytoluene,
used in synthetic fragrances.

00:35:28.580 --> 00:35:29.830
It must be Arata!

00:35:31.120 --> 00:35:33.500
I gave that to him as a gift.

00:35:33.840 --> 00:35:35.000
Where is he?

00:35:36.130 --> 00:35:37.590
Mao's room.

00:35:38.210 --> 00:35:40.680
It's six floors up. That's not far.

00:35:45.890 --> 00:35:48.270
C'mon, Shion, notice!

00:35:53.020 --> 00:35:54.980
No! It's too risky!

00:35:55.270 --> 00:35:57.030
I can't just leave him there.

00:35:58.030 --> 00:36:01.400
Isn't it time we all do
what we can with what we've got?

00:36:02.780 --> 00:36:06.700
Alright, fine!
Shion, you save Shindo!

00:36:06.830 --> 00:36:07.830
Understood.

00:36:18.590 --> 00:36:22.380
It's that crafty analyst! Not on my watch!

00:36:39.650 --> 00:36:42.150
Our Pillbug's under attack.

00:36:42.490 --> 00:36:43.820
Is it going to make it?

00:36:43.950 --> 00:36:46.950
It may be outnumbered, but I modded it.

00:37:33.000 --> 00:37:34.210
Damn it!

00:37:37.000 --> 00:37:38.250
Azusawa!

00:37:39.460 --> 00:37:40.840
What's wrong, Obata dear?

00:37:40.960 --> 00:37:42.800
That hag's interfering with me!

00:37:43.630 --> 00:37:46.130
You lost the upper hand?
That's not like you.

00:37:46.260 --> 00:37:47.640
Shut up, scumbag!

00:37:47.800 --> 00:37:52.220
It'll be fine. You're the best.
You can deal with it.

00:37:53.680 --> 00:37:56.690
Azusawa, you son of a...

00:38:01.480 --> 00:38:02.940
Hey, Pathfinder.

00:38:04.030 --> 00:38:04.900
Sir?

00:38:05.200 --> 00:38:07.570
Head to Arata Shindo's location.

00:38:07.950 --> 00:38:10.490
The governor is acting suspicious.

00:38:11.370 --> 00:38:12.660
Can you go, Vixen?

00:38:13.120 --> 00:38:15.370
Yes. But what about the CID Chief?

00:38:15.500 --> 00:38:18.960
Take care of her later.
It's all been arranged.

00:38:21.540 --> 00:38:25.510
The signal originated
from the Public Safety building.

00:38:27.720 --> 00:38:30.720
Public Safety? What's going on?

00:38:38.310 --> 00:38:39.900
Time's up!

00:38:40.190 --> 00:38:43.110
Wait! The governor's
on her way as we speak!

00:38:43.230 --> 00:38:45.990
No dice. I expect punctuality.

00:38:46.240 --> 00:38:48.360
It's out of my hands now.

00:39:03.170 --> 00:39:04.130
Bureau Chief?

00:39:04.250 --> 00:39:06.050
That's a Pathfinder with her!

00:39:13.430 --> 00:39:14.640
Incoming! Get clear!

00:39:20.650 --> 00:39:21.560
What was that?

00:39:28.490 --> 00:39:30.530
Killing me would be meaningless.

00:39:31.820 --> 00:39:33.660
We decide what is meaningful.

00:39:37.410 --> 00:39:38.710
I'm afraid not.

00:39:39.790 --> 00:39:43.290
I am but a small fragment of this world.

00:39:48.010 --> 00:39:48.800
Don't look!

00:39:58.980 --> 00:40:00.140
Someone just fell!

00:40:00.310 --> 00:40:01.480
Launch the drones!

00:40:01.600 --> 00:40:03.150
Get the governor on camera!

00:40:03.810 --> 00:40:05.190
Suppress the press!

00:40:13.030 --> 00:40:14.160
The Bureau Chief?

00:40:14.660 --> 00:40:15.830
She was killed?

00:40:17.330 --> 00:40:19.160
Did you see that, Governor?

00:40:19.330 --> 00:40:21.910
Someone died because of you!

00:40:22.330 --> 00:40:24.500
Inspector Shindo is next.

00:40:24.630 --> 00:40:27.170
Then come the general personnel.

00:40:42.520 --> 00:40:44.440
Right engine's malfunctioning!

00:40:44.600 --> 00:40:45.690
Keep her up!

00:40:53.910 --> 00:40:56.450
Things are a lot worse than I thought.

00:40:57.830 --> 00:40:59.700
We have to get rid of the drone.

00:40:59.870 --> 00:41:02.210
Get rid of it? How?

00:41:05.790 --> 00:41:09.380
Next task. Activate the
sniper turret at Point B.

00:41:09.880 --> 00:41:10.590
And you?

00:41:11.130 --> 00:41:12.170
Right on time.

00:41:13.510 --> 00:41:14.880
Are you OK?

00:41:17.430 --> 00:41:18.300
Yeah.

00:41:20.970 --> 00:41:23.230
Is it the cigarettes or my age?

00:41:23.730 --> 00:41:24.850
Here we are.

00:41:25.190 --> 00:41:27.810
Emergency kits. You take one, too.

00:41:28.020 --> 00:41:30.320
We don't know what he'll do next.

00:41:30.480 --> 00:41:31.190
Right.

00:41:31.730 --> 00:41:32.650
Let's go.

00:41:39.080 --> 00:41:39.990
There he is!

00:41:45.330 --> 00:41:46.460
Arata!

00:41:48.380 --> 00:41:49.340
Karina!

00:42:00.390 --> 00:42:05.690
I’ve lost so much

00:42:05.810 --> 00:42:13.780
But I’ve promised myself to keep moving on

00:42:19.240 --> 00:42:24.790
Noisy heart beats
Come on, calm down

00:42:24.910 --> 00:42:30.000
I never want to see you broken again

00:42:30.290 --> 00:42:38.970
Take my hand once again

00:42:41.350 --> 00:42:46.770
I’ll never let you go this time

00:42:46.890 --> 00:42:52.110
How can I save you
when I’m scared of falling?

00:42:52.230 --> 00:42:57.570
I have my belief
Still burning red

00:42:57.700 --> 00:43:01.570
Even if my path leads to a cruel truth

00:43:01.700 --> 00:43:05.500
Labels make no sense

00:43:05.620 --> 00:43:09.460
No one should deprive you of who you are

00:43:09.580 --> 00:43:12.920
I just love the way you are

00:43:13.500 --> 00:43:17.090
Are you trembling with fear

00:43:17.220 --> 00:43:21.720
Of the monster that eats up everything?

00:43:21.840 --> 00:43:27.980
We’ve shared the same destiny

00:43:28.100 --> 00:43:30.060
Let’s go together
